# What `gcloud run deploy --source .` uploads. Without this file gcloud falls back to
# .gitignore - which excludes requirements-api.txt, and the Dockerfile COPYs it, so the
# image build failed on staging. Patterns follow gitignore semantics; a leading slash
# anchors a pattern to the upload root (without it, `docs/*` also ate
# web/src/dashboard/docs/ and the build died on a missing module).
/.git
/.github
/.venv
/.cache
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/node_modules
/web/dist
/web/dist-pages
/web/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
/web/tsconfig.node.tsbuildinfo
/stf-cad
/docs/*
!/docs/assistant
/tests
/mosquitto
/utils
# `*.md` is anchored below (`/*.md`): an unanchored `*.md` follows GITIGNORE semantics here
# (any depth) and ate web/public/copilot/docs/**.md - the dashboard Docs page's documents,
# 404 on the live site (2026-10-26). The leading slash keeps only the ROOT markdown out.
# The same trap applies to Cloud Build's docker builder, which applies the sibling
# .dockerignore with the same any-depth matching, unlike a local Docker Desktop build
# (where `*.md` matched root only).
/*.md
!/docs/assistant/*.md
.env
.env.*
.data
/kimi-code/
/.claude/
/.ruff_cache/
/.pytest_cache/
/*.log
/papers/
/deploy/
